  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 225 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nThe upper level low will slowly cross northern Iowa into \nsouthern Minnesota overnight Tuesday night into Wednesday. A \nshortwave, rotating around the western periphery of this \nfeature, will approach northern Nebraska Wednesday night into \nThursday morning. This will bring a slight chance for showers, \nmainly north of the interstate. At the same time, a southern \nstream disturbance will track from the southern Rockies into the\nsouthern plains. Precipitation in association should remain \nwell south of the forecast area. Expect dry conditions to \ncommence beginning Thursday afternoon, continuing through \nMonday. Highs will generally be in the middle to upper 50s into \nthe weekend with 60s possible early next week. The latest NBM is\non the cool side of the guidance envelope and falls short of \nthe ECX and MEX guidance.",
